WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.550 --> 00:00:04.060
This is a tool to calculate how much an
exclusive distribution costs:

2
00:00:04.110 --> 00:00:08.200
the kind done with a fleet dedicated to a
single client. With a month of orders,

3
00:00:08.250 --> 00:00:12.430
it tells you which vehicles would have gone out
each day, what it would have cost,

4
00:00:12.480 --> 00:00:14.500
and what each delivered carton is worth.

5
00:00:15.150 --> 00:00:19.040
It runs on three inputs. The item
master, with the weight,

6
00:00:19.090 --> 00:00:23.390
volume and units per carton of each
product. The vehicle master,

7
00:00:23.440 --> 00:00:26.380
with the capacity in kilos
and cubic meters,

8
00:00:26.430 --> 00:00:29.920
the shift and the cost of each
type of truck or van.

9
00:00:29.970 --> 00:00:34.880
And the list of orders to deliver, with
date, address, item and quantity.

10
00:00:35.530 --> 00:00:41.230
Each address is placed on the map. From
there, the tool works day by day.

11
00:00:41.880 --> 00:00:42.570
For each day,

12
00:00:42.620 --> 00:00:47.010
it gathers the deliveries and builds trips by
grouping the stops that are close

13
00:00:47.060 --> 00:00:47.520
together.

14
00:00:47.570 --> 00:00:49.600
But a trip cannot grow without limit.

15
00:00:49.650 --> 00:00:52.530
It is cut as soon as one of three
limits is reached:

16
00:00:52.580 --> 00:00:57.200
the kilos the vehicle can carry, the volume of
the box, or the length of the shift,

17
00:00:57.250 --> 00:01:01.420
counting driving and unloading. When no
other stop fits, a new trip starts.

18
00:01:01.470 --> 00:01:04.290
Each trip gets the cheapest
vehicle that can do it,

19
00:01:04.340 --> 00:01:08.230
and then the order of the stops is
improved to spend fewer kilometers.

20
00:01:08.880 --> 00:01:13.440
This is what a full day looks like: five
trips, each with its vehicle,

21
00:01:13.490 --> 00:01:17.590
its stops and its cost. The routes are
drawn over real streets.

22
00:01:18.240 --> 00:01:22.090
Repeated for the twenty-two days of the
month, it gives the total cost,

23
00:01:22.140 --> 00:01:24.560
the cost of each day and the
cost per carton.

24
00:01:24.610 --> 00:01:28.410
And it lets you compare different fleets,
to see which one is cheaper.

25
00:01:29.540 --> 00:01:31.740
Adding administration, margin and taxes,

26
00:01:31.790 --> 00:01:35.330
it gives the value per carton that can
be offered to the client.

27
00:01:35.380 --> 00:01:39.040
Exclusive distribution, calculated
before going out on the street.
